    "result_text": "The full test suite is `AcceptanceTest` (the only test class), and it passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule: `membershipTier` is `'GOLD'` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members after the create, otherwise the existing BRONZE/SILVER rules apply.\n\nFollowing the existing pattern (`namesakeCount`, `bulkSignupWarning` are computed at create time and persisted, with the tier derived on the entity), I:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (column `household_size`) with getter/setter, and updated `getMembershipTier()` to return `\"GOLD\"` first when `householdSize >= 3`, falling back to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after `householdId` is assigned, set `householdSize` via a new `householdSize(householdId)` helper that counts existing owners sharing the same non-null `householdId` and adds one for the owner being created (a non-shared owner is a household of one). Persisting the snapshot at create time means the value is available both in the create response and on later `GET` fetches from the DB \u2014 matching how the \"after this create\" wording works and mirroring `namesakeCount`.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `household_size` column, required because `ddl-auto` is `none` and the schema is created from `schema.sql`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` (which was previously failing since no GOLD logic existed) now passes, and the full suite is green.",
